<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Curtius Rufus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Curtius Rufus was a Roman historian, probably of the 1st century CE, author of the Histories of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in ten books, of which the first two are lost. Drawing on earlier Greek sources, his work is one of the main surviving accounts of Alexander's campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It reports that the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanda-dynasty">Nanda dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> was a barber.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quintus-curtius-rufus.jpg" alt="Quintus Curtius Rufus" width="320" height="513" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_de_Grote_te_paard_Titelpagina_voor_Quintus_Curtius_Rufus,_Historia_Alexandri_Magni,_1664,_RP-P-1996-227.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Indian and Greek sources agree that the first Nanda was of humble origin: the Puranas call him the son of a Shudra woman, and the Roman historian <b>Quintus Curtius Rufus</b> reports that the founder of the dynasty was a barber.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Kingdom of Magadha · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Africa. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p></section>
